<div class="entry-content single-content">
	
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">In a small bathroom, the wall above the toilet is often one of the largest empty surfaces you have. It sits right at arm&#8217;s height, it&#8217;s out of your walking path, and in most homes it holds nothing but a piece of art or a bare wall.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">These over the toilet storage ideas turn that space into real storage. Below you&#8217;ll find a quick comparison of the main storage types, a measuring guide so you buy something that actually fits, and 18 ideas, from no-drill options for renters to built-in looks for homeowners.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" width="1024" height="1024" src="https://dailyspacehacks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/a-slim-white-over-the-toilet-storage-cabinet-wit-1.jpg" alt="Slim white over-the-toilet storage cabinet with open shelves above a toilet" class="wp-image-529" srcset="https://dailyspacehacks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/a-slim-white-over-the-toilet-storage-cabinet-wit-1.jpg 1024w, https://dailyspacehacks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/a-slim-white-over-the-toilet-storage-cabinet-wit-1-300x300.jpg 300w, https://dailyspacehacks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/a-slim-white-over-the-toilet-storage-cabinet-wit-1-150x150.jpg 150w, https://dailyspacehacks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/a-slim-white-over-the-toilet-storage-cabinet-wit-1-768x768.jpg 768w, https://dailyspacehacks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/a-slim-white-over-the-toilet-storage-cabinet-wit-1-530x530.jpg 530w, https://dailyspacehacks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/a-slim-white-over-the-toilet-storage-cabinet-wit-1-750x750.jpg 750w, https://dailyspacehacks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/a-slim-white-over-the-toilet-storage-cabinet-wit-1-500x500.jpg 500w" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>



<div class="wp-block-group dsh-summary has-background" style="border-radius:12px;border-left-color:#8FA689;border-left-width:5px;background-color:#EEF3EC;padding-top:20px;padding-right:24px;padding-bottom:20px;padding-left:24px"><div class="wp-block-group__inner-container is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-0d2d72cd wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Key Takeaways</strong></p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>Quick answer:</strong> For most bathrooms, choose a freestanding étagère for renters or wall shelves and cabinets for a built-in look. Measure toilet width, tank height, lid clearance and wall width first, and keep heavy items on low shelves.</li>


<li>Leave enough room above the tank to lift the lid off, and keep the water supply valve reachable.</li>



<li>Keep heavy items low and use an anti-tip strap on freestanding units.</li>
</ul>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Time:</strong> 30 minutes–2 hours · <strong>Cost:</strong> $20–150+ · <strong>Difficulty:</strong> Easy</p>
